name:Oratio Deus, a quo et Judas;
office-part:Oratio;
book:Text Missale O.P. (1939), p. 166; inflexion marks (flex sign and colons) from Officium Hebdomadæ Sanctæ / Triduum O.P. (1927), p. 181-182;
commentary:Set to the Dominican tone for orations at Vespers, Lauds and Mass (Processionarium O.P. 1913, pp. 404-406). Rubric: "absque Dóminus vobíscum, et absque Flectámus génua, præmisso tantum Orémus, dicat Orationem" (Missal p. 166), Orémus is op13-quad6f-oremus;
